---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../data/providers.json';

const roleNames = [['shape', 'Shape'], ['build', 'Build'], ['review', 'Review']];
const detail = (entry) => (entry.state === 'role verified' ? ` (${entry.model}, ${entry.effort})` : entry.state === 'connection tested' ? ` (${entry.model}, ${entry.effort}, ${entry.date})` : '');
---
<Base title="Providers — Kogen" description="Compare every provider name the Kogen CLI accepts: the account or key each needs, the state of each role and where to set it up.">
<main id="main" class="wrap"><article class="prose providers"><p class="eyebrow">Providers</p><h1>Providers Kogen accepts.</h1><p class="lead">Every provider name the Kogen CLI accepts, with the account it needs and the state of each role with its evidence.</p>
<p>Each role is configurable, connection tested or role verified. Only a role verified pair is backed by a qualification record; treat the others as experimental.</p>
<p>The QwenCloud Build evidence came through the fleet proxy; the direct public-install Build is still under test.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="provider-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Account or key needed</th><th scope="col">Roles</th><th scope="col">Built in or custom</th><th scope="col">Instructions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{data.providers.map((provider) => (<tr><td><code>{provider.name}</code></td><td>{provider.account}</td><td><ul class="role-states">{roleNames.map(([key, label]) => (<li>{label}: {provider.roles[key].state}{detail(provider.roles[key])} <a href={provider.roles[key].evidence}>evidence</a></li>))}</ul></td><td>{provider.kind}</td><td><a href={provider.instructions.href}>{provider.instructions.label}</a></td></tr>))}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="small">Start with <a href="/get-started/">Get started</a>.</p></article></main>
</Base>
